  # C.14.4 — actor exit clean-marker sidecar helpers.
  #
  # The auto-generated actor poll loop (PASS_ACTOR) calls __qz_actor_mark_clean
  # immediately before channel_close on both clean-exit paths (tag=-1 stop and
  # tag=-4 cascade stop). The supervisor's watcher calls __qz_actor_check_clean
  # after detecting channel_closed(inbox) to consume the marking — absence
  # means "this close did NOT come from a clean self-stop," treated as crash
  # for Transient restart semantics.
  #
  # Implementation: fixed-size 4096-slot i64 array (32KB, L1-resident), single
  # mutex, full O(N) linear scan on both ops. Chosen over linear-probe hashmap
  # because the chain-break delete is awkward without tombstones, and the
  # working set (bounded by close-rate × supervisor-read-latency) is tiny —
  # full scan completes in <1us, dwarfed by mutex acquisition. If the table
  # ever saturates (pathological close burst with stalled supervisor),
  # mark_clean silent-drops, degrading missed marks to CRASH semantics
  # (safe — Permanent restarts regardless, Transient errs toward restart).
  codegen_util::cg_emit_line(out, "define void @__qz_actor_mark_clean(i64 %amc.inbox) nounwind {")
  codegen_util::cg_emit_line(out, "amc_entry:")
  codegen_util::cg_emit_line(out, "  %amc.nz = icmp ne i64 %amc.inbox, 0")
