  # __qz_sched_register_proc(pid, task): register child pid for exit-wakeup.
  # Linux: pidfd_open(pid, 0) → fd, then epoll_ctl ADD with EPOLLIN|EPOLLONESHOT.
  #   The pidfd is stored in io_map[fd] with task, and pidfd_set[fd]=1 so the
  #   poller closes it after firing. If pidfd_open fails (kernel < 5.3 or pid
  #   already reaped), we set io_map[err_slot] = task and write to the wakeup
