  #   (i.e. exits); the callback posts a kind=3 completion to our IOCP, the
  #   poller dispatches as kind=Process → __qz_sched_reenqueue. A bad HANDLE
  #   (or one that's already signaled before the call) is handled by Win32 —
  #   the threadpool fires the callback immediately and the task re-enqueues
  #   without going through the poller's wait. Mirrors the macOS kevent_imm
